   "tutor": "The rule: start each sentence with a capital letter, write I as a capital, and end with a full stop.\nRight: \"Today I saw a big ship.\" Wrong: \"today i saw a big ship\" The wrong one starts with a small t, writes i small, and has no full stop.\nWorked example: \"The zoo opens on Sunday.\" First, I make the first letter a capital T. Next, I look for the word I; there is none. Last, I add a full stop.\nNow follow the same three steps. Rewrite correctly: \"my brother likes tea\"",
